1
00:03:09,570 --> 00:03:13,449
Shan, you've been
really strong all these years.

2
00:03:13,449 --> 00:03:14,200
There he is.

3
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:14,992
Hey.

4
00:03:16,827 --> 00:03:18,120
I want to go to college already.

5
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:20,122
I’m just looking forward
to that freedom.

6
00:03:20,122 --> 00:03:26,379
Is it really freedom,
or are you escaping?

7
00:03:27,046 --> 00:03:28,339
What's the difference?

8
00:03:29,798 --> 00:03:31,312
For me, they're both the same.

9
00:03:31,328 --> 00:03:32,955
I'm not the type of guy who commits.

10
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:38,736
Let me guess, girl number 1,569.

11
00:03:39,991 --> 00:03:41,743
Shan, the heartbreaker.

12
00:03:42,616 --> 00:03:44,243
Someday, you'll meet your match.

13
00:03:44,283 --> 00:03:45,272
Do I know you?

14
00:03:45,297 --> 00:03:48,342
Oh, I’m sorry.
Do you want me to remind you?

15
00:03:48,497 --> 00:03:49,665
You're just a stranger to me.

16
00:03:49,830 --> 00:03:51,207
And I love challenges.

17
00:03:51,916 --> 00:03:53,167
You’d know, right?

18
00:03:53,876 --> 00:03:55,127
Because we're the same.

19
00:04:03,219 --> 00:04:04,178
Good morning.

20
00:04:05,137 --> 00:04:06,847
Welcome to Yesterday’s Coffee.

21
00:05:54,438 --> 00:05:57,608
Finally, there are no more monsters here.

22
00:06:20,623 --> 00:06:23,151
You seem quieter today, Shan.

23
00:06:24,494 --> 00:06:26,371
Is something bothering you?

24
00:06:32,317 --> 00:06:34,194
I'm just thinking of my mom.

25
00:06:45,604 --> 00:06:47,898
Her death anniversary is coming up soon.

26
00:06:51,737 --> 00:06:52,651
You know,

27
00:06:53,627 --> 00:06:55,295
I just realized how…

28
00:06:56,888 --> 00:06:58,890
fast everything happened back then.

29
00:07:00,026 --> 00:07:00,944
When...

30
00:07:01,643 --> 00:07:02,977
When she passed.

31
00:07:03,401 --> 00:07:04,694
I understand.

32
00:07:05,903 --> 00:07:08,471
You're still processing
what happened.

33
00:07:09,490 --> 00:07:11,325
Yeah, I guess...

34
00:07:11,325 --> 00:07:12,952
I guess I'm getting there.

35
00:07:13,911 --> 00:07:17,081
But whenever I think about
everything that happened

36
00:07:17,081 --> 00:07:18,471
I still get shocked.

37
00:07:19,576 --> 00:07:22,120
I was so young
when all of it happened.

38
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:26,720
It was a lot to take
for a young boy.

39
00:07:28,259 --> 00:07:31,179
But lately, I realized that

40
00:07:31,983 --> 00:07:34,027
even though Mom left early,

41
00:07:35,365 --> 00:07:36,866
she didn't abandon me.

42
00:07:42,857 --> 00:07:45,860
She made sure that even if she left early,

43
00:07:47,101 --> 00:07:48,602
I wouldn't struggle.

44
00:07:50,622 --> 00:07:52,040
You know Shan,

45
00:07:52,689 --> 00:07:54,982
I'm glad you went to high school here.

46
00:07:55,305 --> 00:07:56,306
At least,

47
00:07:56,331 --> 00:07:58,333
I get to see you from time to time.

48
00:07:58,786 --> 00:08:01,080
Don't treat me as
a School Director, okay?

49
00:08:01,711 --> 00:08:02,754
I’m family.

50
00:08:05,348 --> 00:08:07,433
I really see my sister in you.

51
00:08:11,427 --> 00:08:13,554
How have you been?
How are you?

52
00:08:18,017 --> 00:08:19,727
I'm feeling better now.

53
00:08:20,770 --> 00:08:21,813
Uhm…

54
00:08:21,813 --> 00:08:27,276
Your dad said you're not ready
to face people yet,

55
00:08:27,276 --> 00:08:30,238
And he doesn't
want me to see you yet

56
00:08:30,238 --> 00:08:32,281
while you're still grieving.

57
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:35,493
You know Shan,

58
00:08:35,493 --> 00:08:38,057
I was able to see your mom
before she passed.

59
00:08:38,133 --> 00:08:41,803
She asked me to help
process some documents.

60
00:08:42,625 --> 00:08:43,709
Here they are.

61
00:08:44,882 --> 00:08:47,634
I know you're probably
too young to understand.

62
00:08:48,548 --> 00:08:53,010
This involves your mom's
properties and bank accounts.

63
00:08:53,553 --> 00:08:54,776
Don't worry.

64
00:08:54,971 --> 00:08:57,974
I'll tell you more about it
when you're 18.

65
00:08:59,684 --> 00:09:01,432
Once you turn 21,

66
00:09:01,457 --> 00:09:04,043
we can start processing
the transfer of these,

67
00:09:04,068 --> 00:09:07,071
what your mom left
under your name.

68
00:09:18,411 --> 00:09:19,453
Shan.

69
00:09:23,271 --> 00:09:27,283
This is your mom's last wish.

70
00:09:29,122 --> 00:09:31,040
Always remember Shan,

71
00:09:31,065 --> 00:09:33,401
your mom loved you so much.

72
00:09:33,808 --> 00:09:34,627
Hm?

73
00:09:39,473 --> 00:09:41,049
<i>It's just bittersweet</i>

74
00:09:42,351 --> 00:09:45,634
<i>because it really seemed like</i>
<i>she prepared for the day</i>

75
00:09:46,022 --> 00:09:47,197
<i>she would leave me.</i>

76
00:09:54,678 --> 00:09:57,674
<i>When the properties Mom left</i>
<i>were finally transferred to me,</i>

77
00:09:58,451 --> 00:10:02,163
<i>I thought it was the best time</i>
<i>to sort my life out.</i>

78
00:10:09,962 --> 00:10:11,820
There's a lot of fixing to do.

79
00:10:17,110 --> 00:10:21,023
<i>I want to take care of</i>
<i>and fix the things Mom left me.</i>

80
00:10:27,218 --> 00:10:30,847
<i>In that way… </i>
<i>Maybe I can fix myself too.</i>

81
00:10:46,874 --> 00:10:49,919
- Hey, surprise!
- Hello!

82
00:10:49,919 --> 00:10:51,571
Hi, Shan!

83
00:10:51,596 --> 00:10:53,172
We're here for the house tour.

84
00:10:53,172 --> 00:10:54,423
- And—
- Yeah.

85
00:10:54,423 --> 00:10:55,466
making Hiro jealous.

86
00:10:55,466 --> 00:10:56,592
It's beautiful.

87
00:10:56,745 --> 00:10:58,080
We brought something for you.

88
00:10:58,886 --> 00:10:59,887
Yes...

89
00:11:00,221 --> 00:11:01,364
Wait,

90
00:11:01,389 --> 00:11:02,765
what time is it in Florida now?

91
00:11:02,765 --> 00:11:04,308
Should we call Hiro?

92
00:11:04,793 --> 00:11:06,352
Nah, don't.

93
00:11:06,507 --> 00:11:07,675
He's probably busy.

94
00:11:08,396 --> 00:11:10,606
- It's so beautiful.
- This place is so beautiful.

95
00:11:10,606 --> 00:11:11,785
It's so spacious.

96
00:11:12,441 --> 00:11:13,567
I already want to live here.

97
00:11:14,568 --> 00:11:17,196
Finishings look expensive.

98
00:11:18,447 --> 00:11:19,340
How much?

99
00:11:19,365 --> 00:11:20,741
I'm not selling it, you dumbass.

100
00:11:20,741 --> 00:11:21,951
I just moved in.

101
00:11:22,201 --> 00:11:25,981
Wait, what about your condo in Taft?

102
00:11:26,747 --> 00:11:27,785
I'm keeping it.

103
00:11:28,037 --> 00:11:29,705
This one, and the one in Taft.

104
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:32,733
Both of them are from mom,
so I have no plans on selling them.

105
00:11:33,528 --> 00:11:35,723
- Okay.
- Fine, then what about your coffee shop?

106
00:11:36,061 --> 00:11:37,604
You're opening one soon, right?

107
00:11:38,050 --> 00:11:39,593
Did that come from your mom too?

108
00:11:39,844 --> 00:11:41,106
Let me invest.

109
00:11:42,138 --> 00:11:43,556
Are you serious?

110
00:11:44,265 --> 00:11:47,810
You believe in me that much that
you'd invest in my coffee shop right away?

111
00:11:47,810 --> 00:11:49,918
You're not even sure;
it might go under, you know?

112
00:11:50,176 --> 00:11:51,254
Shan, what are you saying?

113
00:11:51,647 --> 00:11:52,565
It’s you we’re talking about here.

114
00:11:52,565 --> 00:11:54,400
I mean, you have a good view.

115
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,943
You have a good vision
of what you want,

116
00:11:56,277 --> 00:11:58,098
And we've already tasted your pastries.

117
00:11:58,237 --> 00:11:59,488
I've already tasted your coffee.

118
00:11:59,488 --> 00:12:01,432
I'm sure it's gonna be a success for you.

119
00:12:01,457 --> 00:12:02,754
- Yeah, yeah.
- Right?

120
00:12:02,779 --> 00:12:04,573
- He's right.
- Don’t worry, Shan.

121
00:12:05,036 --> 00:12:07,455
So, how much?

122
00:12:08,497 --> 00:12:09,373
Come on!

123
00:12:09,373 --> 00:12:10,666
- Let's be business partners.
- You're so annoying.

124
00:12:10,666 --> 00:12:13,294
Acel, Acel, tell Haze
to stop being so persistent.

125
00:12:13,294 --> 00:12:15,087
Haze, stop, stop.

126
00:12:15,087 --> 00:12:17,131
- Stop annoying him.
- Okay, okay, okay. Fine.

127
00:12:18,090 --> 00:12:19,523
It's kinda crazy though,

128
00:12:19,548 --> 00:12:21,820
your interests have really changed, Shan.

129
00:12:22,477 --> 00:12:24,280
From parties

130
00:12:24,305 --> 00:12:26,098
and sleeping around.

131
00:12:27,224 --> 00:12:28,768
- Changed person.
- You're focused on law school now and—

132
00:12:28,768 --> 00:12:30,430
this, the business stuff.

133
00:12:32,331 --> 00:12:34,249
Maybe I'm...

134
00:12:34,398 --> 00:12:36,358
getting tired of that kind of lifestyle.

135
00:12:37,359 --> 00:12:38,319
Really?

136
00:12:40,546 --> 00:12:41,297
No.

137
00:12:42,156 --> 00:12:43,157
Not completely.

138
00:12:45,006 --> 00:12:47,467
It's hard to let go of something
you've gotten used to.

139
00:12:48,784 --> 00:12:49,695
Okay.

140
00:13:13,729 --> 00:13:14,730
The Americano is good.

141
00:13:14,939 --> 00:13:17,191
Bro, this toasted mallow latte,

142
00:13:17,191 --> 00:13:18,192
this will be your best seller.

143
00:13:18,192 --> 00:13:18,943
I can feel it.

144
00:13:18,943 --> 00:13:20,158
- Really?
- Mhmm. It's delicious.

145
00:13:20,694 --> 00:13:22,446
Where do you get your beans, bro?

146
00:13:22,446 --> 00:13:24,365
Even the Americano tastes rich.

147
00:13:26,107 --> 00:13:27,234
Secret.

148
00:13:29,453 --> 00:13:30,121
Nice.

149
00:13:30,121 --> 00:13:31,330
How about you, ma'am?

150
00:13:31,497 --> 00:13:33,666
Does the matcha meet your standards?

151
00:13:34,208 --> 00:13:35,292
It's good.

152
00:13:35,543 --> 00:13:36,877
But like, what's the milk?

153
00:13:37,090 --> 00:13:38,091
Change it.

154
00:13:38,365 --> 00:13:40,076
Okay. Noted on that.

155
00:13:44,343 --> 00:13:45,094
Neil.

156
00:13:45,301 --> 00:13:46,143
Bro.

157
00:13:47,004 --> 00:13:48,463
Are you still looking for Yanna?

158
00:13:49,306 --> 00:13:51,809
Yup. Still can't find her, but

159
00:13:51,809 --> 00:13:53,435
Hiro seems desperate already.

160
00:13:55,893 --> 00:13:58,103
It's really hard to find someone
who doesn't want to be found.

161
00:13:58,649 --> 00:14:00,359
I mean I tried asking people.

162
00:14:00,359 --> 00:14:01,652
But they haven't seen her though.

163
00:14:02,236 --> 00:14:04,190
But like who are her friends?

164
00:14:04,365 --> 00:14:05,991
I feel like we should start there.

165
00:14:06,016 --> 00:14:08,369
That girl, what’s her name…
Sam.

166
00:14:08,659 --> 00:14:09,577
- Can you check her—
- Right!

167
00:14:09,577 --> 00:14:12,079
Check her socials, check her socials.
You never know, right?

168
00:14:20,926 --> 00:14:21,760
Found her.

169
00:14:22,923 --> 00:14:23,299
But Sam isn’t saying anything?

170
00:14:23,299 --> 00:14:25,221
Looks like she’s also friends with Yanna.

171
00:14:25,246 --> 00:14:26,002
Kierra?

172
00:14:26,271 --> 00:14:27,604
Check the other girl’s profile.

173
00:14:30,318 --> 00:14:31,152
That’s her.

174
00:14:31,916 --> 00:14:32,751
That’s her.

175
00:14:33,581 --> 00:14:35,333
Wait, you know her?

176
00:14:36,038 --> 00:14:37,497
Are you friends with her?

177
00:14:37,646 --> 00:14:39,190
Maybe you can contact her.

178
00:14:39,457 --> 00:14:40,624
Is she your ex or something?

179
00:14:40,774 --> 00:14:41,650
Is she your ex?

180
00:14:41,650 --> 00:14:44,403
Or a fling?

181
00:14:46,723 --> 00:14:48,266
I honestly don’t know, guys.

182
00:14:48,291 --> 00:14:49,751
I honestly don’t know.

183
00:14:50,052 --> 00:14:50,677
Wait!

184
00:14:50,993 --> 00:14:52,870
Oh my god, she’s so your type.

185
00:14:52,870 --> 00:14:54,722
Maybe you’ve dated before.

186
00:14:54,747 --> 00:14:56,874
Or maybe you could date her now

187
00:14:56,874 --> 00:14:59,460
and once you're close,
you can ask her where Yanna is.

188
00:14:59,729 --> 00:15:01,212
Bro, do it for Hiro, right?

189
00:15:01,212 --> 00:15:02,046
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

190
00:15:02,046 --> 00:15:03,005
- That's…
- Do you agree?

191
00:15:03,005 --> 00:15:03,672
I agree.

192
00:15:03,672 --> 00:15:04,548
- I don’t know what—
- Right.

193
00:15:04,924 --> 00:15:05,979
- These are all men.
- Then it’s settled.

194
00:15:06,217 --> 00:15:07,843
That is so diabolical.

195
00:15:07,843 --> 00:15:08,760
Use a girl?

196
00:15:19,351 --> 00:15:21,854
Fix your hair,
it's been like that since earlier.

197
00:15:25,402 --> 00:15:27,321
Are you guys ordering or what?

198
00:15:28,595 --> 00:15:30,597
The barista here is so grumpy.

199
00:15:31,533 --> 00:15:32,910
Should we just leave?

200
00:15:33,089 --> 00:15:36,217
Oh, sorry, you can't leave
since you're already seated.

201
00:15:36,997 --> 00:15:37,873
Okay then,

202
00:15:37,898 --> 00:15:39,567
what do you recommend here?

203
00:15:39,962 --> 00:15:42,506
I think you’ll like the...

204
00:15:43,587 --> 00:15:45,214
Iced Spanish Latte.

205
00:15:45,214 --> 00:15:47,591
Okay, sure. I'll trust you on this.

206
00:15:48,458 --> 00:15:50,001
Just brewed coffee for me.

207
00:15:50,177 --> 00:15:52,221
Iced Spanish Latte and brewed coffee.

208
00:15:52,221 --> 00:15:53,050
- Yes, please.
- Okay.

209
00:15:53,075 --> 00:15:54,576
- By the way,
- Thank you.

210
00:15:54,890 --> 00:15:58,185
you need to order food too.
Can't just have drinks.

211
00:15:58,477 --> 00:16:01,994
See? The grumpy barista
is being demanding, too.

212
00:16:02,019 --> 00:16:03,107
It's okay, come on.

213
00:16:03,107 --> 00:16:04,608
Should we try their pastries?

214
00:16:05,567 --> 00:16:06,693
Looks delicious.

215
00:16:06,718 --> 00:16:08,479
- That one.
- This one.

216
00:16:09,169 --> 00:16:12,172
You know, to be honest,
the menu is really promising.

217
00:16:13,189 --> 00:16:14,523
But I suggest

218
00:16:14,834 --> 00:16:18,337
you add some savory snacks
so not everything here is sweet.

219
00:16:18,455 --> 00:16:19,039
Good point.

220
00:16:19,039 --> 00:16:20,416
Good point.

221
00:16:21,542 --> 00:16:23,158
Actually, you know, earlier

222
00:16:23,637 --> 00:16:25,854
someone was asking me for fries.

223
00:16:26,025 --> 00:16:30,738
Maybe I should add food that's
easy to eat while working or studying.

224
00:16:30,763 --> 00:16:32,861
Right?

225
00:16:32,886 --> 00:16:33,885
That's right. Yeah.

226
00:16:36,611 --> 00:16:38,738
There's still so much I need to fix here.

227
00:16:39,283 --> 00:16:40,451
It's okay.

228
00:16:41,061 --> 00:16:44,606
That's how it is in the beginning,
but you'll get used to it.

229
00:16:46,608 --> 00:16:48,694
Wait, I just remembered.

230
00:16:48,852 --> 00:16:51,104
Someone invited me to this

231
00:16:51,405 --> 00:16:53,949
café business conference next week.

232
00:16:54,350 --> 00:16:56,002
I can't attend but...

233
00:16:56,182 --> 00:16:58,059
if you want,
I'll just give you the invite.

234
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:01,623
It's at Claremont Hotel.

235
00:17:02,750 --> 00:17:03,959
There you go.

236
00:17:03,959 --> 00:17:06,086
Go Shan, that would be a big help to you.

237
00:17:06,111 --> 00:17:07,986
Sure, please.
Send me the details.

238
00:17:08,011 --> 00:17:09,262
Yeah. Sure, sure.

239
00:17:09,631 --> 00:17:13,844
So, is this on the house,
these pastries and coffee?

240
00:17:13,844 --> 00:17:15,095
Oh, you don't have to...

241
00:17:15,095 --> 00:17:15,971
Of course.

242
00:17:15,971 --> 00:17:18,057
- Of course, of course.
- Thank you, thank you.

243
00:17:18,057 --> 00:17:18,922
Of course, not.

244
00:17:20,201 --> 00:17:21,785
Don't forget to tip, okay?

245
00:17:22,394 --> 00:17:23,829
Oh, okay.

246
00:17:23,854 --> 00:17:25,314
Thanks anyway.

247
00:17:26,918 --> 00:17:28,648
I thought we were getting it for free.

248
00:17:48,087 --> 00:17:49,088
<i>Opening a café</i>

249
00:17:49,088 --> 00:17:52,091
<i>gave me something</i>
<i>I can put my heart and soul into.</i>

250
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:55,052
<i>I want to take care</i>
<i>of that business properly.</i>

251
00:17:56,595 --> 00:17:58,537
<i>Because it used to be her café,</i>

252
00:17:58,854 --> 00:18:00,606
<i>it used to be her business.</i>

253
00:18:01,328 --> 00:18:03,330
<i>It was a special place</i>
<i>to her heart.</i>

254
00:18:06,772 --> 00:18:09,381
And I want that to be a

255
00:18:09,586 --> 00:18:12,185
special place for customers too.

256
00:18:13,143 --> 00:18:14,936
And how about you, Shan?

257
00:18:15,406 --> 00:18:18,409
Is the café also a special place for you?

258
00:18:22,329 --> 00:18:26,125
How do you feel when you're at the café?

259
00:18:28,502 --> 00:18:29,834
It feels like...

260
00:18:31,872 --> 00:18:36,138
Somehow, I’m alive.

261
00:19:00,356 --> 00:19:01,982
Seems like the nosy guy isn’t here.

262
00:19:02,828 --> 00:19:03,685
Yes!

263
00:19:03,873 --> 00:19:06,542
Come on, "us" is not even a thing.

264
00:19:06,784 --> 00:19:08,891
What do you mean, not a thing? Look!

265
00:19:08,917 --> 00:19:09,751
Yeah, I...

266
00:19:09,751 --> 00:19:11,044
A friend?

267
00:19:11,295 --> 00:19:13,464
